### IntelliJ HTTP Client file (Tools -> HTTP Client). Start the app first, then run top to bottom.
### Assumes a fresh start so the first address book and buddies get id 1, 2, ...

### 1. Create an address book
POST http://localhost:8080/api/addressBooks
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 2. Create buddies
POST http://localhost:8080/api/buddyInfos
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Alex", "phoneNumber": "613-555-0101"}

###
POST http://localhost:8080/api/buddyInfos
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Jordan", "phoneNumber": "613-555-0102"}

### 3. Add buddy 1 to address book 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/addressBooks/1/buddies
Content-Type: text/uri-list

http://localhost:8080/api/buddyInfos/1

### 4. Add buddy 2 to address book 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/addressBooks/1/buddies
Content-Type: text/uri-list

http://localhost:8080/api/buddyInfos/2

### 5. Check the buddies of address book 1 (JSON)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/addressBooks/1/buddies
Accept: application/json

### 6. Thymeleaf view of address book 1 (open in a browser)
GET http://localhost:8080/addressbook/1
